# Camera originals. 23GB, and git is the wrong tool for them — they are irreplaceable but they
# never change, so they need a BACKUP, not version history. Keep them off the index deliberately.
#
# NOTE THE PATTERN: `src/*` and not `src/`. Git cannot re-include anything beneath an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so `src/` would also swallow the .gitkeep markers that exist to make these folders
# survive a clone — the pipeline writes into them and would otherwise fail on a fresh checkout.
# Exclude the contents, keep the directory, re-admit the marker.
src/*
!src/.gitkeep

# Everything a render wrote. Reconstructible from src/ + scripts/, and measured in gigabytes.
dist/*
!dist/*/
dist/*/*
!dist/*/.gitkeep

# Generated LUTs from the search that found the shipped one. The parameters that produce them live
# in look.json, and scripts/make-tone-lut.py stamps them into each cube's TITLE, so the files
# themselves are reproducible output.
luts/tone/variants/
luts/filmic/*.cube

# Apple's LUT archive — redistributable only via Apple's own download (see luts/apple/SOURCE.txt).
luts/apple/*.zip

.DS_Store
*.partial

# Belt-and-braces: no video or camera-raw file ever belongs in this repo, wherever it lands.
# GitHub rejects files over 100MB outright and warns over 50MB; a single clip here is 0.4-2GB.
# Both cases: this repo is on a case-insensitive volume, so *.mov already catches IMG_0609.MOV
# here — but a clone onto a case-sensitive filesystem would not, and the camera does write
# uppercase. Costs nothing to be explicit.
*.mov
*.MOV
*.mp4
*.MP4
*.m4v
*.avi
*.mkv
*.braw
*.r3d

# Stabilisation transforms — multi-MB per clip, regenerated by scripts/00-stabilise-detect.sh
*.trf

# Apple's conversion LUTs are NOT redistributable. They come from Apple's developer downloads
# under the Apple Developer Agreement, and this repo is public — committing them would be
# redistribution. Anyone can fetch them in two minutes with a free Apple ID; luts/apple/SOURCE.txt
# says exactly how, and the pipeline fails with that pointer if they are missing.
luts/apple/*.cube
luts/apple/*.zip

# Backup copies of generated LUTs — regenerate from the parameters in look.json.
*.cube.prev
.workdir

# Python byte-cache. Appears the moment anything imports a script in scripts/ or tests/.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Working notes: specs and tickets for work in progress. The substance belongs in a commit message,
# docs/BACKLOG.md or an ADR by the time the work lands, so this is deliberately disposable.
.scratch/

# Agent worktrees. `git worktree add` under the repo root puts a second full checkout INSIDE the
# working tree, so it shows up as 22MB of untracked files and would be committed by a careless
# `git add -A`. Ignoring the path does not affect the worktree itself — git tracks that in
# .git/worktrees — so `git worktree list` still finds it and its branch is unaffected.
#
# Deliberately NOT a blanket `.claude/`: project-scoped agent config (settings.json, commands,
# skills) belongs in version control if it is ever added, and a broad rule here would silently
# swallow it.
.claude/worktrees/

# Map screenshots used as colour corroboration in docs/PIPELINE.md. Google and Apple both
# restrict redistribution of their map imagery, and the Street View capture carried a visible
# "© 2026 Google" watermark — same constraint as Apple's LUTs above, and this repo is public.
# They were committed once and purged from history; ignoring the paths is what stops a re-add.
# docs/reference-maps-SOURCE.txt has the coordinates to pull them up again locally.
docs/reference-apple-maps.png
docs/reference-street-view.png
